REPRODUCED 2026-09-16 while fixing a-piece-that-slides-inside-an-icon-that-grows-sl.

Cause: a frame clips by default (Layer.clipsContents returns isFrame when nothing was set), and SVGExport.answer returns .picture("a group that cuts off what sticks out of it") for any group that clips. EditorState.exportSVG exports a frame through PhotonzDocument.frameDocument(id:), which keeps the frame itself as the root LAYER, so the whole icon goes out through the picture path as one base64 PNG. MotionSVG.wrap still runs on that picture layer, so a motion on the FRAME would still animate the bitmap, but every motion inside the frame is baked into the pixels and lost. The unmoved list is empty, so ExportDialog's "what the file could not carry" line says nothing.

Possible answers: export a frame's CHILDREN as the document (the frame becomes the viewBox and the background rect, which it already knows how to write in SVGExport.surface) rather than keeping the frame as a clipping layer; or write a clipping group as <clipPath> so it stays shapes. The first is smaller and is what a frame means on export anyway.

Run as Tests/PhotonzRenderTests/ZZProbeTests.swift (deleted after; paste back to re-run):

import CoreGraphics
import Foundation
import PhotonzCore
import Testing
@testable import PhotonzRender

@Suite("probe")
struct ZZProbeTests {
    @Test func whatAnAnimatedIconInAFrameExportsAs() throws {
        var dot = Layer(name: "Dot", content: .annotation(AnnotationContent(shape: .rectangle, strokeWidth: 0, colorHex: "#000000", start: .zero, end: CGPoint(x: 10, y: 10), fillColorHex: "#000000")), frame: CGRect(x: 4, y: 4, width: 10, height: 10))
        dot.motions = [LayerMotion(property: .position, from: .point(CGPoint(x: 4, y: 4)), to: .point(CGPoint(x: 14, y: 4)), timing: MotionTiming(startMS: 0, durationMS: 500), curve: .linear, repeats: .forever)]
        let icon = Layer(name: "Icon", content: .group(GroupContent(children: [dot], isFrame: true, backgroundHex: "#FFFFFF")), frame: CGRect(x: 0, y: 0, width: 32, height: 32))
        var document = PhotonzDocument(canvasSize: CGSize(width: 64, height: 64), layers: [icon])
        document.motionCycleMS = 1000
        let target = try #require(document.frameDocument(id: icon.id))
        let result = SVGExporter.export(target, store: ImageStore(), animation: .moving(cycleMS: 1000))
        print("=== FALLBACKS:", result.fallbacks.map { "\($0.layerName): \($0.reason)" })
        print("=== UNMOVED:", result.unmoved.map { "\($0.layerName): \($0.reason)" })
        print("=== has animate:", result.text.contains("<animate"))
        print("=== has base64:", result.text.contains("base64"))
    }
}

